Hey, does this door look familiar to you?

8
00:01:34,974 --> 00:01:37,174
Yes, it looks more than familiar.

9
00:01:37,714 --> 00:01:39,314
It even has a nameplate.

10
00:01:39,774 --> 00:01:41,734
This doesn't fit here at all! No!

11
00:01:49,654 --> 00:01:50,484
What?

12
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:51,548
It really is my blood!

13
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:54,671
Even the garbage I forgot to take
out is here in perfect detail!

14
00:01:54,754 --> 00:01:56,131
What is up with that goddess?

15
00:01:56,214 --> 00:01:59,214
I really don't understand
what this skill is about.

16
00:02:01,894 --> 00:02:06,247
Right now, all I can think about is
getting you back to your place safely.

17
00:02:06,494 --> 00:02:07,324
I see.

18
00:02:07,434 --> 00:02:08,391
It's because of what I said.

19
00:02:08,474 --> 00:02:11,291
the manner in which she
grants wishes is a little bit

20
00:02:11,374 --> 00:02:15,451
sloppy well the water and

21
00:02:15,534 --> 00:02:18,471
electricity both work but the

22
00:02:18,554 --> 00:02:22,451
TV not so much the windows
don't open and it's pitch

23
00:02:22,534 --> 00:02:26,914
-black outside still a pretty
useful ability though you know

24
00:02:30,134 --> 00:02:34,487
those bites are enormous I'm reminded
of a hamster more than anything else

25
00:02:34,954 --> 00:02:35,784
Well,

26
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:39,871
at any rate, at least we won't have trouble
finding food or a decent place to sleep.

27
00:02:39,954 --> 00:02:40,784
Hmm?

28
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:42,711
Food will be a problem though, won't it?

29
00:02:42,794 --> 00:02:43,624
Hmm?

30
00:02:43,707 --> 00:02:45,171
This is all I have in the house.

31
00:02:45,254 --> 00:02:46,084
All gone.

32
00:02:47,014 --> 00:02:48,214
The last food?

33
00:02:48,554 --> 00:02:49,774
The last food.

34
00:02:51,014 --> 00:02:52,794
You only have one serving?

35
00:02:52,954 --> 00:02:55,791
Why the heck would you
casually eat it right now?

36
00:02:55,874 --> 00:02:57,834
Well, I mean, I was hungry.

37
00:03:02,094 --> 00:03:04,491
You have nothing set
aside for emergencies?

38
00:03:04,574 --> 00:03:07,231
No, because I never eat
at home, don't you get it?

39
00:03:07,314 --> 00:03:10,111
What were you planning to do if there
were a giant earthquake or something?

40
00:03:10,194 --> 00:03:13,841
I knew if that happened, you'd
come and save me anyway, right?

41
00:03:16,274 --> 00:03:19,098
It's all your fault for
being so overprotective!

42
00:03:19,374 --> 00:03:22,134
Then hurry up and become
independent, idiot.

43
00:03:24,454 --> 00:03:27,983
We do have water, so we should
be able to manage for a week.

44
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:31,671
Worst case scenario, we could break
down that bear thing for meat.

45
00:03:31,754 --> 00:03:34,691
There's no way I'm ever going
to eat something like that.

46
00:03:34,774 --> 00:03:37,303
My god, you really are
spoiled, aren't you?

47
00:03:37,834 --> 00:03:40,191
Well, none of this changes
what we have to do.

48
00:03:40,274 --> 00:03:42,333
Gather information and secure food.

49
00:03:42,574 --> 00:03:44,574
We should move while we still can.

50
00:03:44,934 --> 00:03:47,551
You mean we have to keep
hiking up that mountain?

51
00:03:47,634 --> 00:03:50,458
No, I think we'll be done
with that fairly soon.

52
00:03:50,714 --> 00:03:53,831
Actually earlier while we were
being chased I saw some smoke.

53
00:03:53,914 --> 00:03:56,502
I think there might be
a settlement that way

54
00:04:00,694 --> 00:04:02,534
It's so fantasy-esque.

55
00:04:02,794 --> 00:04:04,970
It definitely doesn't look like Japan

56
00:04:05,614 --> 00:04:07,434
But how can I put it?

57
00:04:08,454 --> 00:04:10,674
I'd be okay dressed like this.

58
00:04:12,434 --> 00:04:15,794
I wish I could approve, but I can't.

59
00:04:16,374 --> 00:04:19,271
It's not like I'm wearing this
because I want to, you know!

60
00:04:19,354 --> 00:04:22,731
I only had these because my sister
left them behind when she visited!

61
00:04:22,814 --> 00:04:23,644
That's true.

62
00:04:23,727 --> 00:04:25,302
There's nothing to be done.

63
00:04:26,534 --> 00:04:27,674
I don't get it.

64
00:04:27,794 --> 00:04:31,371
Do you realize you've been pretty
cold to me ever since this happened?

65
00:04:31,454 --> 00:04:33,042
I've always been like this.

66
00:04:33,654 --> 00:04:36,571
Maybe you're self-conscious
since you've got this new body.

67
00:04:36,654 --> 00:04:37,484
Do you think?

68
00:04:38,334 --> 00:04:39,194
Yeah, I guess.

69
00:04:40,814 --> 00:04:44,051
But it's still hard to look at
you, so you need new clothes ASAP.

70
00:04:44,134 --> 00:04:44,964
I know.

71
00:04:45,234 --> 00:04:48,646
We need to hurry up and find
some clothes from this world.

72
00:04:50,814 --> 00:04:53,094
Do it just as we planned. Got it.

73
00:04:53,454 --> 00:04:57,611
I'm a rich young lady from a remote region
and you're here with me as my attendant.

74
00:04:57,694 --> 00:04:59,511
And I can't say why I'm traveling,

75
00:04:59,594 --> 00:05:02,011
but that explains why I
don't know this area at all.

76
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:03,565
And that's all she wrote.

77
00:05:04,134 --> 00:05:06,252
Yeah, sure, that sounds about right.

78
00:05:08,134 --> 00:05:09,434
Just watch and learn.

79
00:05:09,714 --> 00:05:13,871
With this beauty and my great
communication skills, I'll be unstoppable.

80
00:05:13,954 --> 00:05:16,191
I can make any man out
there fall in love with me.

81
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:17,104
Oh, yeah

82
00:05:17,514 --> 00:05:19,334
You never succeed with women?

83
00:05:24,394 --> 00:05:27,100
It's true those looks
will prove advantageous!

84
00:05:28,314 --> 00:05:29,991
Even without knowing the language.

85
00:05:30,074 --> 00:05:31,931
It's unlikely things will go poorly.

86
00:05:32,014 --> 00:05:33,896
Tachibana is a good communicator

87
00:05:37,974 --> 00:05:41,031
Isn't that too much smoke
for such a small settlement?

88
00:05:41,114 --> 00:05:42,674
And it smells charred.

89
00:05:43,334 --> 00:05:44,634
We've got bandits!

90
00:05:47,534 --> 00:05:48,364
Run!

91
00:05:48,534 --> 00:05:49,946
Leave everything behind!

92
00:05:50,954 --> 00:05:51,784
Mommy!

93
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:52,734
Mommy, no!

94
00:05:53,274 --> 00:05:54,104
Help!

95
00:05:55,234 --> 00:05:56,064
Tachibana!

96
00:05:59,494 --> 00:06:00,974
What's the commotion?

97
00:06:01,254 --> 00:06:02,171
Are they having a festival?

98
00:06:02,254 --> 00:06:03,934
Out of the way!

99
00:06:07,834 --> 00:06:10,614
Ma 'am, now my clothes are dirty.

100
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:16,594
You're not hurt, are you, young miss?

101
00:06:17,754 --> 00:06:20,654
Oh, I'm sorry to bother
you while you're working.

102
00:06:20,954 --> 00:06:23,425
It's just that I'm a little lost, you see.

103
00:06:25,874 --> 00:06:26,704
Huh?

104
00:06:26,834 --> 00:06:28,893
Oh, do you maybe not understand me?

105
00:06:30,054 --> 00:06:31,394
Bonjour! Excusez-moi!

106
00:06:33,974 --> 00:06:37,174
Is...is this...could this be...true love?

107
00:06:38,554 --> 00:06:39,874
Ah! No!

108
00:06:41,474 --> 00:06:43,945
Wait...uh...is this a dangerous situation?

109
00:06:44,274 --> 00:06:46,156
I thought you were a woodcutter!

110
00:06:47,114 --> 00:06:48,574
Will you marry me?

111
00:06:49,354 --> 00:06:50,184
Say what?

112
00:06:50,354 --> 00:06:52,451
I'd quit thieving if it were for you!

113
00:06:52,534 --> 00:06:54,851
I'm fully prepared to live a decent life!

114
00:06:54,934 --> 00:06:56,751
We can grow vegetables or something!

115
00:06:56,834 --> 00:06:58,246
And I want two children!

116
00:06:58,494 --> 00:07:00,434
What is this all of a sudden?!

117
00:07:01,054 --> 00:07:02,311
Now that that's settled,

118
00:07:02,394 --> 00:07:05,911
I'll get permission from the boss
and head back to my home country!

119
00:07:05,994 --> 00:07:06,824
Hey!

120
00:07:06,907 --> 00:07:07,737
Hang on a sec!

121
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,451
Whoa, whoa, why are you
playing around over here?

122
00:07:09,534 --> 00:07:10,454
Big bro, look!

123
00:07:10,594 --> 00:07:13,154
I've just found myself
a cute wife! A wife?

124
00:07:13,254 --> 00:07:14,901
What are you going on about?

125
00:07:15,154 --> 00:07:16,374
Will you marry me?

126
00:07:17,014 --> 00:07:17,844
Why?

127
00:07:18,114 --> 00:07:19,991
I'd quit thieving if it were for you.

128
00:07:20,074 --> 00:07:22,011
And I'm prepared to live a decent life.

129
00:07:22,094 --> 00:07:23,871
We can make clay pots or something.

130
00:07:23,954 --> 00:07:25,483
And I want eight children.

131
00:07:25,714 --> 00:07:27,991
How many kids do these
guys want me to have?

132
00:07:28,074 --> 00:07:29,894
So this is what that meant?

133
00:07:30,294 --> 00:07:31,874
Is that what's going on?

134
00:07:32,534 --> 00:07:35,634
My beauty really pushes people this far?

135
00:07:36,114 --> 00:07:37,934
No one steals my wife away!

136
00:07:38,154 --> 00:07:39,448
Not even you, big bro!

137
00:07:39,594 --> 00:07:41,071
She will spend her life with me!

138
00:07:41,154 --> 00:07:43,414
This calls for a duel! Marry me.

139
00:07:43,654 --> 00:07:45,551
I'd quit thieving if it were for you.

140
00:07:45,634 --> 00:07:46,464
No, you won't!

141
00:07:46,547 --> 00:07:47,377
Back off!

142
00:07:48,294 --> 00:07:50,176
What do you think you're doing?!

143
00:07:58,074 --> 00:07:59,074
This is my fault!

144
00:07:59,294 --> 00:08:00,529
Please stop fighting!

145
00:08:00,754 --> 00:08:02,151
This is all so pointless!

146
00:08:02,234 --> 00:08:03,822
I'm not gonna marry anyone!

147
00:08:04,034 --> 00:08:06,014
Are you safe, Tachibana?

148
00:08:06,514 --> 00:08:07,894
Not for my sake.

149
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:09,514
Not for me.

150
00:08:10,174 --> 00:08:12,514
I bet you don't fight!

151
00:08:16,314 --> 00:08:17,214
Oh, wow.

152
00:08:17,714 --> 00:08:18,734
Did you do this?

153
00:08:18,994 --> 00:08:20,534
I haven't done anything.

154
00:08:20,794 --> 00:08:22,031
All I did was exist.

155
00:08:22,114 --> 00:08:24,114
But I... I...

156
00:08:24,694 --> 00:08:28,034
They started fighting because
I'm just too beautiful.

157
00:08:28,894 --> 00:08:29,724
Tachibana.

158
00:08:30,514 --> 00:08:32,867
You're actually loving this, aren't you?

159
00:08:34,994 --> 00:08:37,234
Thank you, O 'Beautiful!

160
00:08:37,914 --> 00:08:39,931
Thank you, O 'Beautiful!

161
00:08:40,014 --> 00:08:43,351
And now it seems I'm being revered
like I'm some kind of deity.

162
00:08:43,434 --> 00:08:47,131
Well, it's a whole lot healthier than
that fight that broke out earlier.

163
00:08:47,214 --> 00:08:51,626
I really have become a woman of such
beauty that I couldn't possibly exist.

164
00:08:52,274 --> 00:08:55,039
I just thought I might
be a little bit popular.

165
00:08:55,214 --> 00:08:56,794
I underestimate it, too.

166
00:08:57,434 --> 00:09:01,316
I think I finally kind of understand
why you started hating women.

167
00:09:01,774 --> 00:09:03,094
Huh? What? No!

168
00:09:04,814 --> 00:09:08,634
Because if this stuff happens
everywhere I go, that'll be... Oh!

169
00:09:08,874 --> 00:09:10,471
And maybe I should hide my face?

170
00:09:10,554 --> 00:09:12,574
Well, does it work? No.

171
00:09:13,834 --> 00:09:16,775
But some countermeasures
do seem like a good idea.

172
00:09:16,934 --> 00:09:19,871
Now that I think about it, why
doesn't it affect you, though?

173
00:09:19,954 --> 00:09:20,784
Hm?

174
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:23,814
Uh, you mean why am I fine
when these guys aren't?

175
00:09:25,894 --> 00:09:28,694
Must be because I know
you're a man. I see.

176
00:09:29,174 --> 00:09:31,233
I'm not exactly unaffected, though.

177
00:09:32,254 --> 00:09:35,711
Maybe it's got something to do with the
intelligence setting and the parameters?

178
00:09:35,794 --> 00:09:38,251
I bet it's got some kind of mental effect.

179
00:09:38,334 --> 00:09:39,164
Crap!

180
00:09:39,247 --> 00:09:40,077
We're defeated!

181
00:09:40,294 --> 00:09:43,034
To think we'd get wiped
out by a lone woman.

182
00:09:44,814 --> 00:09:48,051
But you'd do well to be afraid,
because we're an advance party.

183
00:09:48,134 --> 00:09:49,814
So in just a few hours,

184
00:09:49,974 --> 00:09:51,891
the main group will realize
something's wrong and they'll

185
00:09:51,974 --> 00:09:54,391
get ready to fight and then
they'll come here for you!

186
00:09:54,474 --> 00:09:55,951
We haven't said a single word.

187
00:09:56,034 --> 00:09:58,271
They're having a
conversation with themselves.

188
00:09:58,354 --> 00:10:00,431
I'm really looking forward
to seeing this entire

189
00:10:00,514 --> 00:10:03,251
village get crushed into
the ground like a grave!

190
00:10:03,334 --> 00:10:05,631
If they're close enough to
guess something's wrong,

191
00:10:05,714 --> 00:10:07,949
that means their stronghold is nearby.

192
00:10:11,674 --> 00:10:13,254
Are these guys for real?

193
00:10:13,854 --> 00:10:14,694
Where is it?

194
00:10:15,054 --> 00:10:16,191
You think I'm stupid?

195
00:10:16,274 --> 00:10:17,104
I'm not telling you!

196
00:10:17,187 --> 00:10:18,214
Tachibana?

197
00:10:18,574 --> 00:10:21,034
Well, you give me no choice.

198
00:10:24,254 --> 00:10:26,494
I really wish you'd tell me!

199
00:10:31,754 --> 00:10:33,174
Could it be that...

200
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,534
I'm undefeatable.

201
00:10:35,854 --> 00:10:37,091
What are you waiting for?

202
00:10:37,174 --> 00:10:38,004
Let's go.

203
00:10:39,014 --> 00:10:40,294
So cute!

204
00:10:45,254 --> 00:10:47,734
Well, I guess they would have lookouts.

205
00:10:48,214 --> 00:10:50,038
Seems our enemies aren't fools.

206
00:10:50,234 --> 00:10:53,171
I do like that we can check
their strengths ahead of time.

207
00:10:53,254 --> 00:10:55,814
Uh, you can see other people's stats, too?

208
00:10:56,734 --> 00:10:59,134
Their numbers are low compared to yours.

209
00:10:59,394 --> 00:11:02,331
The thing is, we don't know
how far we can trust these.

210
00:11:02,414 --> 00:11:04,649
And we can't know how many are inside.

211
00:11:05,014 --> 00:11:06,308
We'll tread carefully.

212
00:11:06,554 --> 00:11:07,794
That's no fun at all.

213
00:11:08,254 --> 00:11:09,991
Why don't you just smack
him around a little

214
00:11:10,074 --> 00:11:12,591
bit and finish this up
before it gets started?

215
00:11:12,674 --> 00:11:15,011
You took out that beam
shooting bear with one punch.

216
00:11:15,094 --> 00:11:15,924
You can do it.

217
00:11:16,074 --> 00:11:17,545
You make it sound so easy

218
00:11:18,274 --> 00:11:20,931
Back when you were student council
president you took out a den

219
00:11:21,014 --> 00:11:24,934
of delinquents same thing right
different danger level entirely

220
00:11:26,474 --> 00:11:28,091
Also, I didn't take them out.

221
00:11:28,174 --> 00:11:29,511
I just rehabilitated them.

222
00:11:29,594 --> 00:11:30,994
You call that rehab

223
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,154
Well, then should I go?

224
00:11:33,894 --> 00:11:34,724
Seriously?

225
00:11:34,807 --> 00:11:37,651
What can you do with those
cannon fodder level stats?

226
00:11:37,734 --> 00:11:40,931
Don't go thinking that cannon
fodder isn't good for anything, Mr.

227
00:11:41,014 --> 00:11:41,844
Elite.

228
00:11:42,594 --> 00:11:46,131
Trust me, I'm gonna go crush
their group dynamics completely.

229
00:11:46,214 --> 00:11:47,920
So you're one of those women.

230
00:11:48,114 --> 00:11:50,431
Have you already forgotten
you were almost kidnapped?

231
00:11:50,514 --> 00:11:52,194
Best case, you'd be married.

232
00:11:52,454 --> 00:11:53,934
Worst case, they own you.

233
00:11:54,274 --> 00:11:56,215
You say some really scary things.

234
00:11:56,814 --> 00:12:00,520
How about you just leave this to
me and go ahead to your place?

235
00:12:01,194 --> 00:12:02,051
Uh, I don't know.

236
00:12:02,134 --> 00:12:03,171
It doesn't feel right.

237
00:12:03,254 --> 00:12:07,783
No matter how strong you are, it's not
cool letting you go face danger alone.

238
00:12:08,474 --> 00:12:09,304
Tachibana.

239
00:12:09,974 --> 00:12:10,851
There's just...

240
00:12:10,934 --> 00:12:13,111
there's this part of you that's so...

241
00:12:13,194 --> 00:12:14,534
how can I put it?

242
00:12:14,954 --> 00:12:16,514
So thoughtful and kind.

243
00:12:20,034 --> 00:12:22,152
It's fine, you can leave this to me.

244
00:12:22,434 --> 00:12:24,022
I can find a way on my own.

245
00:12:24,574 --> 00:12:25,633
I'll make it work.

246
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:27,714
Do things for others.

247
00:12:28,214 --> 00:12:31,271
be willing to sacrifice
yourself to make that happen.

248
00:12:31,354 --> 00:12:33,060
That's just how I was raised.

249
00:12:33,454 --> 00:12:35,219
I've never even questioned it.

250
00:12:35,354 --> 00:12:36,431
And yet...

251
00:12:36,514 --> 00:12:39,749
Man, they're making you handle
all the paperwork again?

252
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:41,424
Tachibana?

253
00:12:41,554 --> 00:12:43,731
There's supposed to be two
of you doing this, right?

254
00:12:43,814 --> 00:12:45,285
So where's the other guy?

255
00:12:45,414 --> 00:12:46,649
He's a team practice.

256
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:48,291
He ran out on you, huh?

257
00:12:48,374 --> 00:12:50,091
And now they're just using you.

258
00:12:50,174 --> 00:12:51,527
Come on, hand him over.

259
00:12:52,654 --> 00:12:56,291
I'm in the going home club, and when
I get there, I got nothing to do.

